WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.812
Unit 1 compares runs.

2
00:00:01.812 --> 00:00:06.371
The kit's comparison sorts
every test into new, regressed,

3
00:00:06.371 --> 00:00:11.124
fixed, still open, no longer
evaluated, changed or unchanged.

4
00:00:11.124 --> 00:00:13.500
New is a finding that wasn't there before.

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.812
Regressed is a pass that now fails.

6
00:00:15.812 --> 00:00:18.912
Fixed now passes, and
still open still fails.

7
00:00:18.912 --> 00:00:22.426
No longer evaluated is
the one that matters most.

8
00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:25.185
It's a finding that's
now skipped, planned,

9
00:00:25.185 --> 00:00:28.113
unable to evaluate, or
missing from the run.

10
00:00:28.113 --> 00:00:30.454
It isn't fixed, and counting it as fixed

11
00:00:30.454 --> 00:00:33.400
would turn a lost connection
into remediation.

12
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.688
So fix the run, and run it again.

13
00:00:35.688 --> 00:00:40.223
And one more rule: a new tool release
adds tests and moves every denominator,

14
00:00:40.223 --> 00:00:43.807
so the kit refuses to compare
runs from different versions

15
00:00:43.807 --> 00:00:47.090
until someone records that
they reviewed the change.
